Description:
  Installs Rack::Attack with default security rules to block common
  vulnerability scans and throttle abusive requests.

  Default protections:
    - Bans an IP for 7 days after 3 scanner paths in 10 minutes: PHP files,
      WordPress paths, sensitive files (.env, .git, /etc/passwd), backup
      archives (.zip, .sql, .tar.gz) and common scanner targets
    - Bans an IP for 1 day after 600 requests in 5 minutes
    - Throttles general requests (300/5min per IP; assets and Active Storage exempt)
    - Throttles login attempts (5/20s per IP on POST --login-path)
    - Safelists localhost
    - Logs every refusal as an [ATTACK] line

Examples:
  rails g maquina:rack_attack
  rails g maquina:rack_attack --login-path /sign_in
